# DiskANN/Vamana build hyperparameters tuned for GIST-1M (960-d L2).
# The defaults in build_paper.env target SIFT-128 and undershoot recall by
# ~20 percentage points on GIST.
#
# These values trace the DiskANN paper Table 4 for GIST-1M (R=128, L=125,
# alpha=1.2 -> Recall@10=0.954) with a small L bump for headroom.
#
# Sizing rationale (vs build_paper.env):
#   - max_degree 96 -> 128: more out-edges per node so the graph stays
#     navigable in 960-d space, where each point has many near-equidistant
#     neighbours and a sparser graph stalls in local minima during search.
#   - build_search_list_size 200 -> 200 (kept): paper uses L=125; 200 gives
#     a small graph-quality margin without paying the 4x build-time cost
#     of L=500.
#   - alpha 1.4 -> 1.2: the alpha-pruning rule keeps fewer "long" edges in
#     high-dim; 1.2 is the value the paper recommends when graph diameter
#     starts dominating recall.
#   - pq_chunks 16 -> 64: 960-d / 15-d-per-chunk = 64 chunks. With pq_chunks=16
#     each chunk would span 60 dims, blowing up PQ approximation error and
#     capping recall regardless of search_list_size. chunk_dim=15 strikes a
#     balance between PQ accuracy and PQ-comparison cost during traversal.
#   - build_ram_limit_gb 8 -> 16: larger graph + PQ codebook need headroom.
#
# Expected wall-clock vs build_paper.env: ~1.3-1.5x. On a 64-thread box GIST
# built with paper cfg in 1638 s; this cfg is expected around 35-45 min.

MAX_DEGREE=128
BUILD_SEARCH_LIST_SIZE=200
ALPHA=1.2
PQ_CHUNKS=64

NUM_THREADS=64
BUILD_RAM_LIMIT_GB=16

HASH_SEED=42
